WEBVTT

00:04:29.396 --> 00:04:33.636
These amazing, strong,
small-scale family farmers,

00:04:33.676 --> 00:04:34.956
the majority women,

00:04:34.956 --> 00:04:36.236
are doing it rough.

00:04:36.756 --> 00:04:39.196
They don't have enough food
to feed their families,

00:04:39.196 --> 00:04:40.796
and it's a real crisis.

00:04:41.516 --> 00:04:43.036
What happens is

00:04:43.036 --> 00:04:46.036
they go out and plant fields of cassava
when the rains come.

00:04:46.076 --> 00:04:47.756
Nine months later,

00:04:47.796 --> 00:04:50.876
there's nothing, because of these
pests and pathogens.

00:04:50.916 --> 00:04:53.076
And I thought to myself,

00:04:53.076 --> 00:04:56.276
how in the world can farmers be hungry?

00:04:56.796 --> 00:04:59.116
So I decided to spend
some time on the ground

00:04:59.156 --> 00:05:00.836
with the farmers and the scientists